# Modern JavaScript Over jQuery

**Avoid jQuery unless absolutely necessary.** Use modern JavaScript APIs and ES6+ features instead for better performance, smaller bundle sizes, and improved maintainability.

## **DOM Selection & Manipulation**

### ✅ DO: Use Modern JavaScript
```javascript
// Element selection
const element = document.querySelector('.my-class');
const elements = document.querySelectorAll('.my-class');
const elementById = document.getElementById('my-id');

// Adding/removing classes
element.classList.add('active');
element.classList.remove('inactive');
element.classList.toggle('visible');
element.classList.contains('active');

// Setting attributes
element.setAttribute('data-value', 'example');
element.removeAttribute('data-old');

// Content manipulation
element.textContent = 'New text';
element.innerHTML = '<span>New HTML</span>';
element.value = 'New input value';

// Style manipulation
element.style.display = 'none';
element.style.backgroundColor = '#ff0000';
```

### ❌ DON'T: Use jQuery equivalents
```javascript
// Avoid these jQuery patterns
$('.my-class');
$('#my-id');
$element.addClass('active');
$element.removeClass('inactive');
$element.toggleClass('visible');
$element.hasClass('active');
$element.attr('data-value', 'example');
$element.text('New text');
$element.html('<span>New HTML</span>');
$element.val('New input value');
$element.hide();
$element.css('background-color', '#ff0000');
```

## **Event Handling**

### ✅ DO: Use addEventListener
```javascript
// Single event listener
element.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    // Handle click
});

// Event delegation
document.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
    if (event.target.matches('.button')) {
        // Handle delegated click
    }
});

// Multiple events
['mouseenter', 'mouseleave'].forEach(eventType => {
    element.addEventListener(eventType, handleMouseEvent);
});

// Remove event listener
element.removeEventListener('click', clickHandler);
```

### ❌ DON'T: Use jQuery event methods
```javascript
// Avoid jQuery event handling
$element.on('click', handler);
$element.off('click', handler);
$element.click(handler);
$(document).on('click', '.button', handler);
```

## **AJAX Requests**

### ✅ DO: Use Fetch API
```javascript
// GET request
async function getData(url) {
    try {
        const response = await fetch(url);
        if (!response.ok) {
            throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);
        }
        const data = await response.json();
        return data;
    } catch (error) {
        console.error('Fetch error:', error);
        throw error;
    }
}

// POST request
async function postData(url, data) {
    try {
        const response = await fetch(url, {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: {
                'Content-Type': 'application/json',
                'X-WP-Nonce': wpApiSettings.nonce // WordPress nonce
            },
            body: JSON.stringify(data)
        });
        return await response.json();
    } catch (error) {
        console.error('Post error:', error);
        throw error;
    }
}
```

### ❌ DON'T: Use jQuery AJAX
```javascript
// Avoid jQuery AJAX methods
$.ajax({
    url: '/api/endpoint',
    method: 'GET',
    success: function(data) { },
    error: function(xhr, status, error) { }
});

$.get('/api/endpoint');
$.post('/api/endpoint', data);
```

## **DOM Ready & Loading**

### ✅ DO: Use Modern Approaches
```javascript
// DOM content loaded
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    // Initialize code
});

// Or use modules with defer/async
// In HTML: <script src="app.js" defer></script>

// Check if DOM is already loaded
if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
} else {
    init();
}
```

### ❌ DON'T: Use jQuery ready
```javascript
// Avoid jQuery document ready
$(document).ready(function() {
    // Initialize code
});

// Or shorthand
$(function() {
    // Initialize code
});
```

## **Element Creation & Insertion**

### ✅ DO: Use Modern DOM Methods
```javascript
// Create elements
const div = document.createElement('div');
div.className = 'new-element';
div.textContent = 'Hello World';

// Insert elements
parentElement.appendChild(div);
parentElement.insertBefore(div, referenceElement);
element.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', '<span>New content</span>');

// Remove elements
element.remove();
parentElement.removeChild(element);
```

### ❌ DON'T: Use jQuery creation/insertion
```javascript
// Avoid jQuery element creation
const $div = $('<div class="new-element">Hello World</div>');
$parent.append($div);
$parent.prepend($div);
$element.after($div);
$element.before($div);
$element.remove();
```

## **Animations & Effects**

### ✅ DO: Use CSS Transitions/Animations + JavaScript
```css
/* Define transitions in CSS */
.fade-in {
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
}

.fade-in.visible {
    opacity: 1;
}

.slide-down {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 0.3s ease;
}

.slide-down.open {
    max-height: 200px; /* or use auto with JavaScript calculation */
}
```

```javascript
// Trigger animations with classes
element.classList.add('visible');

// Or use Web Animations API for complex animations
element.animate([
    { opacity: 0, transform: 'translateY(-20px)' },
    { opacity: 1, transform: 'translateY(0)' }
], {
    duration: 300,
    easing: 'ease-out'
});
```

### ❌ DON'T: Use jQuery animations
```javascript
// Avoid jQuery animation methods
$element.fadeIn();
$element.fadeOut();
$element.slideDown();
$element.slideUp();
$element.animate({ opacity: 1 });
```

## **Utility Functions**

### ✅ DO: Use Modern JavaScript Utilities
```javascript
// Array iteration
items.forEach(item => processItem(item));
const processed = items.map(item => transform(item));
const filtered = items.filter(item => item.active);

// Object manipulation
const merged = { ...obj1, ...obj2 };
const keys = Object.keys(obj);
const values = Object.values(obj);

// Type checking
Array.isArray(value);
typeof value === 'string';

// Utilities
const trimmed = str.trim();
const parsed = JSON.parse(jsonString);
const serialized = JSON.stringify(data);
```

### ❌ DON'T: Use jQuery utilities
```javascript
// Avoid jQuery utility methods
$.each(items, function(index, item) { });
$.map(items, function(item) { });
$.extend({}, obj1, obj2);
$.isArray(value);
$.type(value);
$.trim(str);
$.parseJSON(jsonString);
```

## **When jQuery Might Still Be Acceptable**

- **Legacy WordPress plugins** that require jQuery as a dependency
- **Complex UI libraries** (like jQuery UI) where modern alternatives aren't feasible
- **Temporary compatibility** during gradual migration from jQuery codebase
- **Third-party integrations** that specifically require jQuery

**Important:** Even in these cases, isolate jQuery usage and avoid mixing with modern JavaScript patterns.

## **WordPress Specific Considerations**

### ✅ DO: Handle WordPress jQuery Conflicts
```javascript
// If jQuery is absolutely required, use noConflict mode
jQuery(document).ready(function($) {
    // Use $ safely within this scope
});

// Or use WordPress's jQuery wrapper
(function($) {
    // jQuery code here
})(jQuery);
```

### ✅ DO: Enqueue Modern Scripts Properly
```php
// In functions.php - enqueue modern JavaScript
wp_enqueue_script(
    'theme-modern-js',
    get_template_directory_uri() . '/js/app.js',
    [], // No jQuery dependency
    filemtime(get_template_directory() . '/js/app.js'),
    true // Load in footer
);
```

## **Bundle Size & Performance Benefits**

- **Smaller bundles:** Modern JavaScript eliminates jQuery's ~30KB overhead
- **Better performance:** Native DOM APIs are faster than jQuery abstractions
- **Modern features:** Access to latest browser APIs and ES6+ features
- **Better debugging:** Direct browser API usage in developer tools
- **Future-proof:** Aligned with modern web development practices

## **Migration Strategy**

1. **Audit existing jQuery usage** in the codebase
2. **Replace simple DOM operations** first (selectors, classes, attributes)
3. **Convert event handlers** to addEventListener
4. **Replace AJAX calls** with fetch API
5. **Remove jQuery animations** in favor of CSS transitions
6. **Update build process** to exclude jQuery if no longer needed

Refer to [webpack.settings.js](mdc:config/webpack.settings.js) for build configuration and [functions.php](mdc:functions.php) for proper script enqueueing in WordPress.
